// Fixture: cri_delete_composition_crossfield
// Rule under test: GDDL Spec v4 §5.2-§5.3 (composition) + §6.6 (delete templates) +
// §6.7 (cross-field references), all three together in one fixture. Highest-value
// category for this round -- real bugs found so far in this project (operator
// precedence, leading-token parsing) came from combinations, not isolated rules.
//
// `ShapeTemplate` is `delete`-marked, composes a nested `Point` struct (`origin`), and
// computes `area` via a cross-field reference INTO that composed sub-field
// (`origin.x * origin.y`). `RealShape` then copies the template and changes
// `origin.x` -- but does NOT restate `area`.
//
// KEY PREDICTION, STATED EXPLICITLY (grounded in already-established behavior, not a
// fresh guess, but non-obvious enough to be worth spelling out): `area` should NOT
// recompute. GDDL expressions are evaluated once, eagerly, at their own point in
// strictly sequential execution (§6.2, and directly confirmed by
// sequential_crossfield_reference_sees_current_value.gddl in this same round) --
// there is no "live formula" mechanic anywhere in the spec. Copying an instance
// carries forward already-RESOLVED values, not unevaluated expressions to be
// re-run later. So `RealShape.area` should still read 25 (5*5, computed once inside
// `ShapeTemplate`), even though `RealShape.origin.x` is now 10, not 5. If a reference
// implementation instead produces 50 (10*5, as if `area`'s formula re-ran against the
// new `origin.x`), that would reveal an unexpected live-recomputation behavior nothing
// in the spec currently describes -- worth flagging back rather than just noting as a
// "bug" if it happens, since it could equally mean a real, previously-undocumented
// rule exists that this corpus hasn't caught up to yet.

define Point
	x = u32
	y = u32

define Shape
	origin = Point
	area   = u32

Shape ShapeTemplate delete
	origin
		x = 5
		y = 5
	area = origin.x * origin.y
	// cross-field reference reaching into a composed sub-field, inside a delete
	// template -- computed once, here, against origin's values at this exact point.

Shape RealShape = ShapeTemplate
	origin
		x = 10
		// y untouched -> inherited 5
	// area: NOT restated. Per the prediction above, this should carry forward
	// ShapeTemplate's already-computed value (25), not recompute against the new x.

// Expected (prediction, pending golden output from Compiler Core reference run --
// see the key prediction stated in detail above):
//   Compiles cleanly, no error.
//   ShapeTemplate: not present in exported output (delete-marked).
//   RealShape.origin == { x: 10, y: 5 }
//   RealShape.area   == 25   (NOT 50 -- see key prediction above for why)
